<%# locals: (address:, user:, badges: nil, compact: false) %>
<%#
  ONE WALLET, SHOWN AS A PERSON WHERE THERE IS ONE — AND AS AN ADDRESS ALWAYS.

  THE ADDRESS IS NEVER REPLACED BY THE NAME. An operator opens this page to
  decide which key to remove, and what he removes is a base58 key. So the full
  address renders on every row whether or not a user was found; the name sits
  above it as a reading aid and nothing more. That ordering is the whole design:
  identity is an ADDITION to the address.

  AN UNHELD WALLET SAYS SO, OUT LOUD. Most addresses on this page are agent and
  operator keys and nothing guarantees any of them is an app account. Rendering
  a miss as a blank name, or as the same coloured initials circle a real account
  gets, would read as "an account we know, whose name we did not bother to
  print" — and a wrong identity here is worse than no identity. So the miss gets
  a DASHED ring, muted ink and the words, all three of which differ from every
  resolved row at a glance.

  WHICH COLUMN MATCHED IS PART OF THE ANSWER. This app keeps one user's wallet
  in either of two places, and saying which one matched is what lets the
  operator tell a Phantom he can be asked to sign with from a managed wallet
  this server holds the key to.
%>
<% wallet_kind = user && (user.web3_solana_address == address ? "Phantom" : "Managed") %>

<div class="flex min-w-0 items-start gap-2">
  <% if user %>
    <%= render "components/avatar", user: user, size: "sm" %>
  <% else %>
    <%# NOT AN AVATAR, AND IT MUST NOT LOOK LIKE ONE — no fill, a dashed ring,
        and the same muted ink the words below it use. %>
    <span aria-hidden="true"
          class="mt-px flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full
                 border border-dashed border-strong text-3xs font-bold text-muted">
      ?
    </span>
  <% end %>

  <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-1.5 gap-y-0.5">
      <% if user %>
        <span class="truncate text-xs font-bold text-heading"><%= user.display_name %></span>
        <span class="rounded bg-surface-alt px-1 py-px text-3xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">
          <%= wallet_kind %>
        </span>
      <% else %>
        <span class="text-xs font-medium text-muted">No linked account</span>
        <span class="rounded border border-dashed border-strong px-1 py-px text-3xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">
          Unresolved
        </span>
      <% end %>
      <%= badges %>
    </div>

    <p class="font-mono text-2xs text-secondary break-all" data-wallet-address><%= address %></p>

    <%# ONLY THE MISS GETS A SENTENCE. A resolved row has already said everything
        it has to say — a face, a name and the wallet kind — and repeating "held
        by an account" under each one buries the row that ISN'T. The unresolved
        case is the one an operator has to be told about explicitly, because a
        quiet row reads as an ordinary one. %>
    <% if user.nil? && !compact %>
      <p class="text-3xs text-muted">
        No Turf Monster account holds this address on either wallet, so this
        page can put no name to it. Evict it by the address above.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
